From: Joel Gerber <Jitsusama@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Finish a collection a long call has outgrown

Qt 6.12.0's incremental collector steps a cycle on only from the event
loop, in slices of a few milliseconds, and runGC() returns at once while
one is running. So through one long call, every allocation that misses
takes a new chunk, and a chunk is freed only once wholly empty: each
stays held by the few objects the call kept in it. A shell hearing a
1.4 MB answer in one call of about a second grew its heap from 34 to
93 MB, and held all of it for the rest of its run. Once the heap has
grown by half since the running cycle began, the limit Qt already puts
on the unmanaged heap during a cycle, the cycle is now finished at the
allocation, as that limit's is.

---
--- a/src/qml/memory/qv4mm.cpp
+++ b/src/qml/memory/qv4mm.cpp
@@ -1363,6 +1363,7 @@ void MemoryManager::runGC()
     }
 
     gcBlocked = MemoryManager::NormalBlocked;
+    slotsAtCycleStart = blockAllocator.totalSlots() + icAllocator.totalSlots();
 
     if (statistics) {
         statistics->maxAllocatedMem
--- a/src/qml/memory/qv4mm_p.h
+++ b/src/qml/memory/qv4mm_p.h
@@ -476,8 +476,16 @@ private:
         if (HeapItem *m = allocator->allocate(size))
             return m;
 
-        if (!didGCRun && shouldRunGC())
-            runGC();
+        if (!didGCRun && shouldRunGC()) {
+            // A cycle steps on only from the event loop, so through one long call every miss
+            // took a new chunk, each left holding a few of what the call kept. Once the heap
+            // has grown by half since the cycle began, as the unmanaged heap's limit allows,
+            // the cycle is finished here instead.
+            if (incrementalGCIsAlreadyRunning && outgrewCycle())
+                (void) tryForceGCCompletion();
+            else
+                runGC();
+        }
 
         return allocator->allocate(size, true);
     }
@@ -508,6 +516,13 @@ public:
     std::size_t unmanagedHeapSize = 0; // the amount of bytes of heap that is not managed by the memory manager, but which is held onto by managed items.
     std::size_t unmanagedHeapSizeGCLimit;
     std::size_t usedSlotsAfterLastFullSweep = 0;
+    // The slots the heap held as the cycle now running began.
+    std::size_t slotsAtCycleStart = 0;
+    bool outgrewCycle() const
+    {
+        const std::size_t total = blockAllocator.totalSlots() + icAllocator.totalSlots();
+        return total > 3 * slotsAtCycleStart / 2;
+    }
 
     enum Blockness : quint8 {Unblocked, NormalBlocked, InCriticalSection };
     Blockness gcBlocked = Unblocked;
